{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact self-hosting design draft3 df98081e3957a88e4024859d89c21becaf03b493. Primary read first in full, qualification record reread in full, all prior findings and original conditions checked. No further finding.\n\nF1 resolved as design: section4.7 distinguishes a stopped process from a checked completed drain, requires the stopped session's sealed-close log plus sealed/absent bucket record, preserves VM/work directory/name and refuses replacement/deletion/complete-backup claims on unknown outcomes. Backups include bucket AND every node's work directory and identity/peer addresses; traffic/deploy writers/supervisors stop for the snapshot and leases expire. Persistent disks, restart/stop settings and H4's forced unknown-drain case are explicit across sections5/6/9/10/12. Pinned source confirms the folded log lives in nodes/\u003cnode\u003e.json (node_log.rs516ff) with the process generation and log epoch/state, and a successful seal demands covered retained bundles/per-cell data (5535ff); exit0 alone remains insufficient. The future kit must implement those checks for the actual stopped session, not infer them from a process status.\n\nF2 remains resolved in both documents: observed command-line wall times, unmatched samples and unmeasured runtime/commit components stay explicit; no isolated bucket-cost bound or measured two-node speedup is claimed. F3 remains resolved: optional supported APPLICATION_CONTENT binding/bucket_name/prefix and APPLICATION_TRUST, R2 unavailable without fleet bucket, neither smoke installed packages, H4 owns conditional-put/get/readback. F4 remains resolved as design: ingress-owned CF-Connecting-IP overwrite, loopback-only Worker listener and explicit forged/missing-header plus separate-client witnesses; H1's supplied header is a fixture, not proxy acceptance.\n\nThree conclusions. (1) The production coupling map and pinned celld direction are coherent; replacements stay at host/configuration/serving boundaries and propose no native judgment, entry or replay change. (2) Host self is a bounded host object behind existing RegisterHost/DestinationHost ports, not a new native scope kind; durable Git/token behavior, real clone/push/stale refusal, whole-pack bounds and archive independence remain the named H2/later obligations. (3) The GCP-first/AWS-shaped kit, operator sequence and after-plan033 slices are reviewable, and the record's one-node/in-memory-host/no-alarm limits are honest. Alarms, two-node recovery, failed drain, backup restore, proxy/TLS, package storage, upgrades and AWS remain future qualification, not accepted by this document approval. The recorded cloud runs were assessed as the author's committed report; checker did not independently rerun them or receive their raw logs.\n\nValidation: all2290 leaves checked, all2288 base leaves unchanged and exactly two added notes. Draft2→draft3 changes only the design note; qualification is identical. Fourteen relative links resolve, whitespace passes. Candidate tree87a5488b212addbd4e213f2a394bfd62a19ee8c9; base9554919b treebbabe9a2f6e0d374b845b46f18d9856251ed0b57. Source and tests unchanged: no gate rerun under docs/testing.md's docs-only exception. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-celld-draft3-ur6nwcel/validation.json; pinned upstream source retained at /private/tmp/checker-celld-design-dtwhk47a/upstream, archiveSHA25661c073fc91b26cedc9ba042e9112750657fefee3b442f72626045b159b79b71b. Sources: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/guarantees.md ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/cloudflare-compat.md ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/services/r2.md ; https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/reverse_proxy#headers . No installs, source/ref mutation, push or deployment by checker. Native bound implementation closure still requires its sealed landing receipt; H1/H2 remain behind design approval/plan033 ordering.","body":{"artifact":"git:s